{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 4958062,
  "courseSlug": "remix-course",
  "courseTitle": "Remix.js - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "34674724",
      "title": "Layout Routes",
      "lectureOrder": 39,
      "videoOrder": 35,
      "sourceHash": "d9014a4c3a426b61afdb1abbdab2fca5bcfb22d3101fee863354bee85fb61f1a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.31,
          "end": 5.85,
          "en": "So what are layout routes in Remix?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.85,
          "end": 8.55,
          "en": "The idea behind layout routes is simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.55,
          "end": 10.26,
          "en": "When you're building a website,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.26,
          "end": 13.17,
          "en": "like the website we are about to build here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.17,
          "end": 15.18,
          "en": "then it's quite common,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.18,
          "end": 17.85,
          "en": "it's pretty much always the case, you could say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.85,
          "end": 21.78,
          "en": "that many pages share some common elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 21.78,
          "end": 23.64,
          "en": "like the main navigation bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.64,
          "end": 25.65,
          "en": "It's very common that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.65,
          "end": 27.75,
          "en": "all or at least a lot of your pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.75,
          "end": 29.73,
          "en": "have the same navigation bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 29.73,
          "end": 32.883,
          "en": "They might also have the same footer or anything like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.99,
          "end": 36.87,
          "en": "Now instead of repeating those shared components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.87,
          "end": 40.44,
          "en": "in all your page components, which would be very cumbersome.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 40.44,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "it makes sense to have like a layout component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "that wraps all those other pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 49.62,
          "en": "And you might remember from the essentials section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 49.62,
          "end": 53.79,
          "en": "that we have such a wrapper component that wraps all pages",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 53.79,
          "end": 55.503,
          "en": "the route.JSX file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.52,
          "end": 59.19,
          "en": "You learned in the Remix essentials section",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.19,
          "end": 63.3,
          "en": "that this route.JSX file contains a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 63.3,
          "end": 67.26,
          "en": "the app component - that is loaded for every page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 67.26,
          "end": 69.33,
          "en": "So no matter which page you visit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.33,
          "end": 71.103,
          "en": "this component is always loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.45,
          "end": 75.09,
          "en": "Now, this is very useful because, as you can see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 77.13,
          "en": "this component actually returns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.13,
          "end": 80.55,
          "en": "the actual HTML page structure,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.55,
          "end": 83.1,
          "en": "the HTML wrapper element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 86.31,
          "en": "the head section, and the body section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.31,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "And then you might remember that in the essentials section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 93.9,
          "en": "I mentioned this outlet component, which simply",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 93.9,
          "end": 98.1,
          "en": "marks the place where the actual page component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.1,
          "end": 101.37,
          "en": "which is currently active, should be injected to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.37,
          "end": 104.19,
          "en": "So if we are visiting the pricing page, for example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.19,
          "end": 107.03999999999999,
          "en": "this h1 element would be injected",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 107.03999999999999,
          "end": 108.39,
          "en": "in place of this outlet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.39,
          "end": 111.27000000000001,
          "en": "That's how this wrapper component works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.27000000000001,
          "end": 113.22,
          "en": "The advantage of this wrapper component is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 113.22,
          "end": 115.32,
          "en": "that we can have this shared structure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 115.32,
          "end": 118.5,
          "en": "and that we could of course add more shared content here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 118.5,
          "end": 120.96,
          "en": "We could add some shared head tags,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 120.96,
          "end": 123.21,
          "en": "some meta tags for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 123.21,
          "end": 127.5,
          "en": "besides injecting meta content on a per page basis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 127.5,
          "end": 130.41,
          "en": "as you also learned in the essentials section already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 130.41,
          "end": 132.78,
          "en": "But we could add some shared content here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 132.78,
          "end": 134.64,
          "en": "And we could, of course, also add some",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 134.64,
          "end": 136.98,
          "en": "shared elements here in the body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.98,
          "end": 139.07999999999998,
          "en": "like for example, a shared header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.07999999999998,
          "end": 140.913,
          "en": "That is something we could do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 142.07999999999998,
          "end": 144.39,
          "en": "So this root component here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 144.39,
          "end": 147.36,
          "en": "this app component is very important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.36,
          "end": 150.99,
          "en": "but the more complex your applications get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 150.99,
          "end": 155.28,
          "en": "the more common it is that one shared layout might not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.28,
          "end": 158.37,
          "en": "be enough, because a layout is not just limited to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.37,
          "end": 161.43,
          "en": "sharing a header or a navigation bar.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 161.43,
          "end": 164.01,
          "en": "You could have other elements or features",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.01,
          "end": 167.01,
          "en": "which you might want to share across some pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.01,
          "end": 169.11,
          "en": "but not all pages.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 169.11,
          "end": 172.56,
          "en": "For example, here for the expenses, we could have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 172.56,
          "end": 176.13,
          "en": "the scenario that some user interface feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.13,
          "end": 180.12,
          "en": "some component, should be shared across all expenses pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 180.12,
          "end": 184.74,
          "en": "but not be part of auth and pricing and the home page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 184.74,
          "end": 187.92,
          "en": "And that's why Remix supports nested layouts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 187.92,
          "end": 189.54,
          "en": "which you simply create",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 189.54,
          "end": 193.32,
          "en": "by choosing a file name that matches the path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 193.32,
          "end": 195.45,
          "en": "for which you want to create a layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.45,
          "end": 197.91,
          "en": "So for example, for /expenses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 197.91,
          "end": 202.293,
          "en": "if all expenses pages should then share that layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.19,
          "end": 205.74,
          "en": "And then you create a folder with the same name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.74,
          "end": 209.57999999999998,
          "en": "so all the with expenses that includes all the files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 209.57999999999998,
          "end": 213.3,
          "en": "all the routes that should use that shared layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.3,
          "end": 214.23,
          "en": "So that's important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 214.23,
          "end": 217.18,
          "en": "You put all the files in there that should use this layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.19,
          "end": 220.35,
          "en": "So if you then for example, have one file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 220.35,
          "end": 223.95,
          "en": "like the raw.JSX file, that should actually become active",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 223.95,
          "end": 226.44,
          "en": "for /expenses/raw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 226.44,
          "end": 229.05,
          "en": "but that should not share that layout -",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 229.05,
          "end": 232.17000000000002,
          "en": "in this case for example, because it will later",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 232.17000000000002,
          "end": 235.98,
          "en": "become a route that simply offers us the raw data -",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.98,
          "end": 239.91,
          "en": "then you can move that file out of the expenses folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.91,
          "end": 242.553,
          "en": "and go back to that .notation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.9,
          "end": 248.49,
          "en": "That way, this would still be loaded for /expenses/raw",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 248.49,
          "end": 251.193,
          "en": "but it would not be part of that shared layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.21,
          "end": 256.2,
          "en": "Now, if this shared layout thing is still a bit strange yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 256.2,
          "end": 258.87,
          "en": "that's totally fine, it's just a theory here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 258.87,
          "end": 260.67,
          "en": "We're going to use it in the application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 262.11,
          "en": "throughout this course though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.11,
          "end": 264.63,
          "en": "so things will become much clearer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 264.63,
          "end": 266.13,
          "en": "but it hopefully makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 266.13,
          "end": 268.17,
          "en": "that you might want to have some shared elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 268.17,
          "end": 269.64,
          "en": "across multiple pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 269.64,
          "end": 272.58299999999997,
          "en": "and that this layout feature is what helps you with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 273.63,
          "end": 276.27,
          "en": "So here in this case we could, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 276.27,
          "end": 280.59000000000003,
          "en": "create a shared layout by exporting a default function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.59000000000003,
          "end": 284.433,
          "en": "the expenses layout, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 285.93,
          "end": 288.06,
          "en": "And in there we could now return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 288.06,
          "end": 292.71,
          "en": "let's say, 'main' as a wrapper, doesn't matter too much.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 292.71,
          "end": 296.163,
          "en": "Then here a paragraph where I say shared element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 297.06,
          "end": 301.05,
          "en": "And then below that we again need such an outlet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.05,
          "end": 303.99,
          "en": "such a marker, that tells Remix where",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 303.99,
          "end": 307.95,
          "en": "the actual routes that are using that layout",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 307.95,
          "end": 309.54,
          "en": "should be injected to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 309.54,
          "end": 311.76,
          "en": "So where the content of these nested routes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 311.76,
          "end": 312.963,
          "en": "should be injected to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 313.83,
          "end": 317.49,
          "en": "So therefore here we use outlet, and outlet is a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 317.49,
          "end": 321.603,
          "en": "that must be imported from @remix-run/react.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 322.5,
          "end": 325.44,
          "en": "Now with that, we're using that layout and if we now",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 325.44,
          "end": 329.82,
          "en": "save everything and we reload, we see that shared element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 329.82,
          "end": 332.22,
          "en": "for all these nested expenses pages,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 332.22,
          "end": 335.43,
          "en": "like expenses analysis, or expenses add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 335.43,
          "end": 338.64,
          "en": "or expenses sum ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 338.64,
          "end": 341.31,
          "en": "And also for just /expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 341.31,
          "end": 344.76,
          "en": "because there we load this index.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 344.76,
          "end": 347.67,
          "en": "So the component to find in this index.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 347.67,
          "end": 351.45,
          "en": "in this expenses folder, that is the index route",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 351.45,
          "end": 354.27,
          "en": "for this layout route, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 354.27,
          "end": 356.34000000000003,
          "en": "so for this expenses folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 356.34000000000003,
          "end": 359.94,
          "en": "And that's the content we load if we visit just /expenses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 359.94,
          "end": 363.363,
          "en": "and here we've, of course, also got that shared element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 364.83,
          "end": 368.34,
          "en": "Now, if we enter expenses/raw though",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 368.34,
          "end": 370.41,
          "en": "you don't see the shared element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 370.41,
          "end": 372.84,
          "en": "despite having such a nested path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 372.84,
          "end": 376.937,
          "en": "because I renamed this raw file to expenses.raw.jsx",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 377.97,
          "end": 380.85,
          "en": "and moved it out of the expenses folder.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 380.85,
          "end": 383.883,
          "en": "Therefore it shares the path, but not the layout.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 384.84,
          "end": 387.063,
          "en": "And that's the idea behind these layouts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 388.02,
          "end": 390.24,
          "en": "Now, by the way, just to be clear,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 390.24,
          "end": 394.40999999999997,
          "en": "you can also get rid of that index.jsx file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 394.40999999999997,
          "end": 397.02,
          "en": "If you had some shared element that's needed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 397.02,
          "end": 398.76,
          "en": "by all the nested paths",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 398.76,
          "end": 401.15999999999997,
          "en": "but you don't have any specific content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 401.15999999999997,
          "end": 404.34000000000003,
          "en": "for just /expenses, then you can get rid",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 404.34000000000003,
          "end": 405.99,
          "en": "of that index.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
